I made this poem to try to understand what creators that used to make amazing content.. now just sound ai.. so I tried to imagine what they might have felt,
as every aspect of their creative choices was run thru an optimization machine.. I think that the way things are now incentivise people to give up on their humanity.. and were made to lose the spark that made them start something in the first place and then ai came along.. and they saw a way to rest a bit, and found a new normal. 

what we were or contraction or the algorithm


have we not chased
every challenge
explored every color
fallen in public
then rose alone?

have we not
been every beast
loved every insect
then killed them all?

have we not
won all the battles?
soothed every muscle
broken every bone
a long while ago?

have we not
spilled all our tears
conqured all our fears
gave up all our goals?

there are no wars left to fight
for me
this padded room is all I see
no bones to break
no fears to shake

just prompts
to feed this channel